# The devnet's generated directory, and it is generated ALL THE WAY DOWN: two
# `connector.toml`s, every credential, and — since `pnpm demo` — the MPEG-TS
# segments a viber has bought.
#
# THIS IS THE `.ts` COLLISION CLAUDE.md WARNS ABOUT. An HLS segment is an
# MPEG-TS file with a `.ts` extension, which is also TypeScript's, so
# `deploy/**/*.ts` in the format scripts matches a broadcast. Without this,
# `pnpm format:check` fails for anybody who has run the demo — and it fails by
# printing binary video into their terminal.
#
# Ignored by DIRECTORY rather than by extension, which is the rule the repo
# already follows for `segments/` and `recordings/`: never add a `*.ts` ignore.
deploy/devnet/run/
